<title>UK: British election diary - March 21.</title>
<headline>British election diary - March 21.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the main election campaign events scheduled for Friday.</p>
<p>- Parliamentary prorogation ceremony at which government's record will be set out in House of Lords and retiring MPs will get chance to bid farewell to Speaker, 1100 GMT.</p>
<p>- Morning news conference provisionally with Labour deputy leader John Prescott and chief whip Donald Dewar. Time to be arranged.</p>
<p>- Prime Minister John Major on campaign trip. Time and destination to be announced.</p>
<p>- Labour leader Tony Blair has no public engagements.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7768</p>
</text>
